(6952495, 1046618, 18197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Teafran:</b></div><hr/><i> The problem with lots of snow is that....well, its a picture of a lot of snow. Bland and rather uninteresting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Being from CT, you''d know snow! This is an interesting question of foreground/background. To my eye, it''s not so much a picture of snow, as it''s a picture of woods and stream. But thanks for the comment. Good comments always shake up my thinking as did yours.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Teafran: The problem with lots of snow is that....well, its a picture of a lot of snow. Bland and rather uninteresting.   Being from CT, you''d know snow! This is an interesting question of foreground/background. To my eye, it''s not so much a picture of snow, as it''s a picture of woods and stream. But thanks for the comment. Good comments always shake up my thinking as did yours.', '2013-01-08 13:14:17.000000', NULL, 0),
